#
# Counter-example for the native math:UndeclaredUnsupportedConstruct gate
# (crates/validate/src/lint.rs, check_math_undeclared_unsupported_construct): a LOSSY
# math:ProjectionRecord — it declares a logic:preservationKind other than
# logic:ExactPreservation — that enumerates NO logic:unsupportedConstruct at all. A lossy
# projection drops nothing or names everything it drops; a record claiming loss while
# naming none has claimed a completeness its own preservation kind denies. The native gate
# MUST emit math:UndeclaredUnsupportedConstruct.
#
# The source is a plain math:MathematicalObject, not a math:Distribution carrying a
# parameterization and not a math:MathematicalExpression, so the two FINER unrecorded-drop
# gates (math:ProjectionDroppedParameterization, math:UnrecordedProjectionLoss) have
# nothing to key on and this fixture isolates the coarse obligation: a lossy record must
# name SOMETHING.
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:silentlyLossyProjection a math:ProjectionRecord ;
    math:projectionSource ex:someObject ;
    math:projectionTargetName "OWL annotation (label only)" ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation .

ex:someObject a math:MathematicalObject .
